From 2839b28ce29d6509ac75f9d020510cf9d70941bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:26:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dvc): align declined-channel handling with upstream

Backport Devolutions/IronRDP#2341 (a7ab89bd842baca5aa8b336c7e5d60782201485f) to the 0.6.x APIs. Remember only actual declines/client closes in bounded transport-aware history, settle on server close/reuse and validate all Soft-Sync entries before extending history. Preserve downstream reassembly limits. This base only permits data on tunnels, so upstream tunneled create/close APIs are not introduced.
